Installation

Requirements

To build Graph Switching you need:

  - a C compiler with C99 support, such as GCC or Clang;
  - make; and
  - standard C library headers.

graphswitching-explore additionally requires Python 3, the nauty amtog and
labelg programs, and the standard sort utility at run time. Its optional
automorphism group size filters use dreadnaut.

The install target also uses a POSIX-style install command. nauty and
Traces are optional. They are useful for converting and canonically
labelling generated graphs, and the nauty library enables --sym.

Build

From the repository root, run:

    make

This creates six executables in the repository root:

    graphswitching
    graphswitching-explore
    gen_all_srgs
    gen_all_srgs_64vts
    gen_all_srgs_wqh6
    gen_all_srgs_wqh_generic

Build symmetry support

make checks whether a small nauty program can be compiled and linked. It
first uses pkg-config or the compiler's normal search paths. It also
recognizes the common packaged header locations:

    /usr/local/include/nauty/nauty.h
    /usr/local/include/nauty/schreier.h
    /usr/include/nauty/nauty.h
    /usr/include/nauty/schreier.h

For example, a nauty installation with its header at
/usr/include/nauty/nauty.h and its library in the normal system library
path is detected by an ordinary:

    make

When the check succeeds, graphswitching is built with --sym support. The
option calls nauty directly to compute the input graph's full automorphism
group and the stabilizer orbits required by the selected switching method.
If the check fails, the rest of graphswitching is still built and --sym
reports that nauty support is unavailable.

If the headers or library are in another location, supply them explicitly:

    make \
        NAUTY_CPPFLAGS="-isystem /path/to/nauty" \
        NAUTY_LDLIBS="/path/to/nauty/nauty.a"

NAUTY_HEADER_DIRS can add or replace the automatically searched nauty
header directories:

    make NAUTY_HEADER_DIRS="/opt/nauty/include/nauty"

Set WITH_NAUTY=0 to disable the probe. Set WITH_NAUTY=1 to require nauty
and let compilation fail if it cannot be used:

    make WITH_NAUTY=0
    make WITH_NAUTY=1 NAUTY_CPPFLAGS="..." NAUTY_LDLIBS="..."

API users can enable the same code path by defining
GRAPHSWITCHING_WITH_NAUTY, making nauty.h available, and linking the nauty
library.

To compile with a different compiler or optimization level:

    make clean
    make CC=clang CFLAGS="-O2"

make check builds every executable, exercises the standard command-line
options, compares the default GM method with gen_all_srgs, and compares the
explicit WQH method with the original generic program. It also checks
graphswitching-explore graph6 parsing, canonical round files, limits,
parallel execution, and automorphism filtering with deterministic test
programs.

Install

The default installation prefix is /usr/local:

    sudo make install

Choose another prefix if desired:

    make install PREFIX="$HOME/.local"

For package creation, DESTDIR is supported:

    make install DESTDIR=/tmp/graphswitching-package PREFIX=/usr

Remove installed executables with the same prefix:

    sudo make uninstall

Configure the specialized programs

The graph order is compiled into these three programs:

    code/gen_all_srgs.c
    code/gen_all_srgs_64vts.c
    code/gen_all_srgs_wqh6.c

Edit the #define VTS near the top of the desired file, then rebuild its
target. For example:

    make gen_all_srgs_wqh6

For gen_all_srgs_64vts, VTS must fit in the bit width of INTT; consult the
source comments before changing either definition.

The recommended graphswitching tool infers the graph order by default:

    ./graphswitching < adjacency-matrix.txt

Specify it explicitly or select WQH when desired:

    ./graphswitching --vertices 63 < adjacency-matrix.txt
    ./graphswitching --method wqh --part-size 3 < adjacency-matrix.txt

Use graphswitching-explore for repeated rounds starting from graph6 files:

    ./graphswitching-explore \
        --method wqh --part-size 3 \
        --output-dir switching-closure seeds.g6

The directory must be new or empty. Run ./graphswitching-explore --help for
parallelism, round, time, graph-count, symmetry, and automorphism-filter
options. The program automatically recognizes amtog, labelg, and dreadnaut,
as well as the nauty-prefixed names used by some packages. Explicit command
paths and a common prefix can also be supplied.

Run ./graphswitching --help for the complete interface. The tool supports
n <= 448; WQH supports p <= 8. The original limits remain in
code/gen_all_srgs_wqh_generic.c, while the new interface exposes its limits
and version in include/graphswitching.h.

Clean the build

Remove all generated executables:

    make clean
